---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const UPDATED = "November 4, 2026";
---

<Layout title="Terms & Conditions" description="The terms for using Study Timer Online: acceptable use, timer accuracy limits, third-party content, and liability." canonicalPath="/terms">
  <section class="page-band" style="padding-block: 3rem 6rem;">
    <div class="container-page" style="max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <article class="card legal-copy" style="padding: clamp(28px, 6vw, 56px); border-radius: 28px; line-height: 1.8;">
        <header style="margin-bottom: 2rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--brand-a15); padding-bottom: 1.5rem;">
          <h1 style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem); font-weight: 800; color: var(--content-heading); margin: 0; line-height: 1.2;">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
          <p style="margin: 0.75rem 0 0;">Last updated: {UPDATED}</p>
        </header>

        <p>These terms apply to your use of studytimeronline.com. By using the site, you agree to them. If you don't agree, please don't use the site.</p>

        <h2>1. What the site provides</h2>
        <p>Study Timer Online offers free browser-based tools (a countdown timer, a Pomodoro timer, a daily planner and session statistics) and study guides. We may add, change or remove features at any time.</p>

        <h2>2. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You may use the site for personal, educational and professional purposes. You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>interfere with or disrupt the site or its servers, for example through automated high-volume requests;</li>
          <li>attempt to gain unauthorised access to any part of the site;</li>
          <li>copy and republish the site's guides or design as your own;</li>
          <li>use the contact form to send spam or unlawful content.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Timer accuracy</h2>
        <p>Timers run in your browser. Device sleep, battery-saving modes, closed tabs and browser restrictions on background audio can delay or silence alarms. <strong>Don't rely on the site for safety-critical, medical, cooking, laboratory or other timing where a missed alarm could cause harm or loss.</strong></p>

        <h2>4. Your data</h2>
        <p>Planner tasks and session history are stored only in your browser (see the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>). We can't recover them if your browser data is cleared, and we aren't responsible for their loss.</p>

        <h2>5. Study guides</h2>
        <p>Our guides are general information about study habits, written in good faith. They aren't professional, medical or educational advice for your individual situation.</p>

        <h2>6. Advertising and third-party links</h2>
        <p>The site may show ads served by Google and links to other websites, including our own apps. We don't control third-party sites and aren't responsible for their content or practices.</p>

        <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>The site's text, guides, design and code belong to Study Timer Online. You're welcome to link to any page, and to quote short passages from the guides with a link back.</p>

        <h2>8. Disclaimer and limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>The site is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind. To the fullest extent permitted by law, we aren't liable for any indirect, incidental or consequential loss arising from your use of the site.</p>

        <h2>9. Changes</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms. The date at the top shows when they last changed. Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the updated terms.</p>

        <h2>10. Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about these terms? <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
